//functy:extern

// The barcode function, provided in Go by barcode-cty-func (GetBarcodeFunctions). This
// file declares its signature only — it is never compiled, and nothing here is
// callable.
//
// It exists because cty cannot express the last argument. The options object is
// *optional*, and the only way cty offers to make an argument optional is to make it
// variadic — which says it may be repeated, when it may not. cty also has no way to
// describe the object's shape, so it is declared dynamic: reflected from cty alone the
// function reads as `barcode(type, data, ...options)`, and what may go in that object is
// anybody's guess. Below it has a name, a type, and its four attributes.

// A barcode image, as a PNG `bytes` value (its content type is set to "image/png").
func barcode(
    type: string,  // "qr", "datamatrix", "aztec", "pdf417", "code128", "code93", "code39", "codabar", "ean13", "ean8", or "2of5"
    data: string,  // what is valid depends on the symbology: EAN-13 wants 12 or 13 digits, Code 39 an uppercase alphanumeric subset, QR anything
    // Sizing and encoding options — every attribute is itself optional:
    //
    //   scale             whole-number multiplier on the symbology's natural size (default 4)
    //   width, height     an explicit pixel size instead
    //   error_correction  "L", "M", "Q" or "H" — QR only (default "M")
    //
    // Size the image by `scale`, or by an explicit `width` and `height`. The two are
    // mutually exclusive, since both decide the horizontal size, and `width` requires
    // `height`. `height` alone is allowed, and pairs with a scaled width. Given neither,
    // a 1D symbology gets a conventional bar height and a 2D one is square.
    //
    // Passing `error_correction` with any type but "qr" is an error, not a value
    // silently ignored.
    options?: object({
        scale            = optional(number),
        width            = optional(number),
        height           = optional(number),
        error_correction = optional(string),
    }),
) -> bytes
